{
  "_readme": [
    "Every user-configurable setting in the suite, and where it is allowed to live.",
    "",
    "Two categories, and only two. A setting is either a preference (server-side,",
    "one control, follows the person) or per-browser UI state (deliberately local).",
    "There used to be a third for hosted mode, where Quick Walls, Scale and Report",
    "ran on GitHub Pages with no server to save to. That branching is retired.",
    "",
    "Settings drifted in the first place because there was never a rule: each one",
    "went wherever the tool that needed it already had a habit, and the habit was",
    "set by whether that tool happened to have a server call handy. Merge rule and",
    "refresh interval ended up in BOTH stores, which is how the Settings page came",
    "to show a value that was not in force.",
    "",
    "This file is the rule. tests/test_settings_registry.py enforces it.",
    "Adding a setting means adding it here first."
  ],
  "categories": {
    "preference": {
      "store": "server",
      "definition": "A choice about how the suite behaves for this person. Follows them across browsers and profiles, so it belongs in ~/.wd_wireless_tools/settings.json. Exactly one control anywhere in the suite. There is no second store and no server-when-present fallback: hosted mode is retired, so every tool has a server and every preference lives in one place.",
      "examples": [
        "merge conflict rule",
        "report units",
        "which owners the Files list opens on"
      ]
    },
    "ui-state": {
      "store": "browser",
      "definition": "Where a panel was left, whether a section was expanded, whether a one-time tip has been seen. Deliberately stays in localStorage: syncing a collapsed panel between machines would be a regression, not a feature, and hoovering these onto the Settings page is what would turn it into a long list of toggles nobody wants.",
      "examples": [
        "sidebar width",
        "disclosure open/closed",
        "tip dismissed"
      ]
    }
  },
  "internal": {
    "_comment": "State, not settings. No control, and not expected on the Settings page.",
    "keys": [
      "_version",
      "setup_complete",
      "report.page_orient",
      "report.report_defaults"
    ]
  },
